# Source is always text, even when a file contains a byte git heuristically
# reads as binary.
#
# `src/lib/privacy/hash.ts` used a literal NUL as its `join()` separator, so
# git classified it as binary and showed "Binary files differ" instead of a
# diff — which is how a new function on the PII path reached review unseen
# (PR-42). The byte itself is now an escape, but a diff is only textual when
# *both* sides are, so this makes the classification explicit rather than
# heuristic and stops the next one happening silently.
*.ts   diff
*.tsx  diff
*.mts  diff
*.mjs  diff
*.json diff
*.md   diff
*.sql  diff
